    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, i'm putting together a hypertrophy plan for a client. can u explain the specific role of leucine in triggering the mTOR pathway? also need to know how a caloric surplus specifically impacts nitrogen balance for muscle protein synthesis. thanks.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Leucine acts as a potent activator of the mTOR pathway by binding to and activating Sestrin2, which subsequently downregulates TSC2 and inhibits its ratios, ultimately relieving the inhibition of mTORC1 and initiating muscle protein synthesis. A caloric surplus improves nitrogen balance by providing the abundant energy required to fuel the energetically costly synthesis of new muscle proteins beyond the basal threshold needed for maintenance. When energy availability is high, the body prioritizes building lean tissue rather than breaking it down, ensuring that excess amino acids are efficiently incorporated into muscle fibers during hypertrophy training.",
